course: dictionary
lesson: 8878
title: Shout: loud, urgent and sometimes unkind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Shout» has more than one meaning. Most often it means to say something very loudly, like «Don't shout» in a quiet library. It can also mean to call loudly to get help, as in «Shout for help» when you are in danger.
explain: Look at the words around it to find the meaning. «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air and shouts "dvanAdtsyat!" — twelve!» The waving and the word twelve show he is excited and happy, not cross.
explain: A shout can be frightening too. In Birmingham, Dhruv's mum shouts after a row about homework, and his dad says nothing all evening. Think about how the people feel, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Shout means to say something very loudly, or to call loudly to get attention.
fact: As a noun, a shout is a loud cry, such as «a shout of joy».
fact: In British and Australian informal speech, «It's my shout» means it is someone's turn to pay.
fact: If someone grabs you or you are in danger, shout «No!», «Help!» or «Fire!» loudly and run to a safe adult.
fact: Shouting indoors or at people can be rude or scary, and phrases like «shout at» and «shout down» often show this.
exercise: «Sashko waves his exercise book in the air and shouts "dvanAdtsyat!" — twelve!» Why is he shouting? | *He is excited and happy | He is hiding from a dog | He is cross and wants a fight | He is fast asleep and dreaming
exercise: You are in danger and someone grabs your arm. What should you do? | Whisper quietly and wait | Sit down and say nothing | *Shout «No!» loudly and run to a safe adult | Shout at the person and stay where you are
exercise: At a café your friend says, «It's my shout.» What does this mean? | Please be quiet now | I want to shout at the waiter | It is my turn to sing loudly | *It is my turn to pay
test: «Shout "hello" in a big empty hall and a moment later the walls shout it back.» What is the returning sound called? | *An echo | A shadow | A tint | A shade
test: What does the phrase «shout for help» mean? | To write a letter to a friend | To sing a happy song | To whisper a secret | *To call loudly to get help
exam: Dhruv's mum shouts after a row about homework; why might shouting be frightening? | Shouting always means happy news | *Shouting at people can be rude and scary | Shouting is only used in libraries | Shouting makes everyone quiet and calm
